  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/pes300.html",
  "prefLabel": "Pes 306.05 Sales of Prohibited-Limited Use and Restricted Pesticides",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Pes 306.05 Sales of Prohibited-Limited Use and Restricted Pesticides. Dealers shall not distribute or sell prohibited-limited use or restricted pesticides to persons holding supervisory registration certificate-general use, as defined in Pes 101.36, or to any other person except to persons who hold and present a current restricted use permit to apply pesticides or a current supervisory certificate of registration, other than a supervisory registration certificate-general use, as issued by the division.\n\nSource. #8059, eff 5-30-04; ss by #9924-A, eff 5-10-11; ss by #10198-B, eff 10-3-12; ss by #13363, eff 6-1-22, EXPIRES: 6-1-32",
